1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,150
Buying a downdraught extraction bench is only the start.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:14,060
In Great Britain, local exhaust ventilation must be thoroughly examined and tested at least every 14 months, with records kept for at least five years.

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:18,590
A downdraught bench is local exhaust ventilation, not furniture.

4
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:25,550
A fan draws air down through the work surface and a filter, pulling dust and fume away from the operator.

5
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:35,160
Regulation 9 of COSHH asks for three things: keep the bench clean and in good repair, have it examined and tested, and keep the records.

6
00:00:35,510 --> 00:00:38,390
Fourteen months is a maximum, not a target.

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:47,290
Performance drifts as filters load with dust, as the work on the bench changes, when the surface is blocked, or as the fan wears.

8
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:50,520
Other countries set their own rules.

9
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:58,300
In Singapore, the reference is SS 658 of 2020, the code of practice for local exhaust ventilation.

10
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:04,070
